go 1.27

// The examples live in their own module so that `go get` of the engine never
// pulls example code or assets, while `git clone` still gets everything. This
// workspace makes local edits to the engine resolve for the examples without
// any replace directive -- and go.work is ignored by consumers.
//
// ./x is the module for opinionated systems built on the engine's public seams
// (ADR 0012). The order of these entries is the dependency direction, which the
// module boundaries enforce rather than merely document: the engine requires
// neither of the others, x requires the engine, and the examples require both.
// An engine package that imports x would make the engine depend on its own
// opinions; ximport_test.go fails the build if one does.
use (
	.
	./x
	./examples
)
